      3 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ساحلوا</span></b> , (S, K,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُسَاحَلَةٌ</span>, (TA,) (tropical:)  <i>They
took,</i> (S,) or <i>came,</i> (K,) <i>to the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَاحِل</span> [or <i>shore,</i>
&amp;c., of the sea]. (S, K, TA.) Hence, in a trad.
respecting Bedr, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَسَاحَلَ بِٱلْعِيرِ</span> <i>And he brought
the caravan to the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَاحِل</span> <i>of the sea.</i> (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُوَ يُسَاحِلُهُ</span>, inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَحَالٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُسَاحَلَةٌ</span>, <i>He contends, disputes,</i> or <i>litigates, with him.</i> (TA.)

